## Phase 5 — Final Diagnosis

**Confirmed fault:** Both dswa1 and dswa2 carry a two-rule nftables FORWARD chain on br0.10 (VLAN 10 interface):
1. `l4proto icmp … accept` — ICMP explicitly permitted
2. All other protocols matching `ip saddr 10.1.0.0/24 ip daddr 10.3.0.0/24` → **drop**

dswa2's ICMP-accept counter = **44 packets**, confirming it is the active forwarder for VLAN 10 → VLAN 3 traffic. dswa1 has the same rules (hot-standby path). TCP/UDP application traffic from VLAN 10 toward any 10.3.0.x host will be silently dropped at dswa2 (or dswa1 on failover).

